  "metadata": {
    "title": "Bubble sort: passes, swaps and the growing sorted suffix",
    "subject": "Computer Science",
    "topic": "Bubble Sort Invariant",
    "objective": "Show how larger elements move right and the sorted suffix grows each pass.",
    "learner": "Can read arrays and loops.",
    "misconceptions": [
      "One pass always sorts everything",
      "Swaps are free"
    ],
    "expectedUnderstanding": "Each pass compares only neighbours and moves the largest remaining value one step right per swap, so after pass p the last p cells are final and sorted; the suffix grows by exactly one cell per pass, and only a pass with zero swaps proves the whole array is sorted."
  },
